        "answer": {
          "short": "A rectangular hyperbola with branches in the first and third quadrants, approaching both axes.",
          "worked": "Plot $(-4,-\\frac12)$, $(-2,-1)$, $(-1,-2)$, $(-\\frac12,-4)$, $(\\frac12,4)$, $(1,2)$, $(2,1)$ and $(4,\\frac12)$. Join the points with two smooth branches, one in each of the first and third quadrants. Do not join across $x=0$; neither branch meets an axis.",
